## Routing Architecture

### Public Route Table

| Destination   | Target            |
|---------------|-------------------|
| 10.0.0.0/16   | local             |
| 0.0.0.0/0     | Internet Gateway  |

This subnet is public because it routes 0.0.0.0/0 traffic through an IGW.

### Private Route Table

| Destination   | Target       |
|---------------|--------------|
| 10.0.0.0/16   | local        |
| 0.0.0.0/0     | NAT Gateway  |

The private subnet has no route to the Internet Gateway, preventing inbound internet access.

---

## Security Controls

### Security Groups
- Default Security Group for the VPC.
- Allows inbound traffic only from other resources using the same security group.
- Denies all external inbound traffic.
- Allows all outbound traffic by default.

### Network ACLs
- Default Network ACLs allow all inbound and outbound traffic.
- Stateless traffic filtering at the subnet boundary.
- Can be restricted for additional segmentation if needed.

